<testgrp id="RM000002QX5001X_03_0003" proc-id="RM0550J___00002AT00000">
<testtitle>Radio Wave Environment Check</testtitle>
<content6 releasenbr="1">
<test1>
<ptxt>Hold the electrical key transmitter close to the front passenger side door handle and check the operation.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<ptxt>Communication is not possible within 20cm of the door handle.</ptxt>
</atten3>
<spec>
<title>Specified Condition</title>
<specitem>
<ptxt>Operates normally</ptxt>
</specitem>
</spec>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Holding the electronic key close to the front passenger side door handle makes it less susceptible to radio interference, so it can be determined whether radio interference is the cause.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>If the inspection result is "OK" and the system does not operate only at specific locations or times, radio interference is likely. Also, dealer-installed parts, etc. (mobile phone charger, power outlet [AC100V power supply], etc.) may cause radio interference, so if there are dealer-installed parts, remove them and check the operation.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</test1>
</content6>
<res>
<down ref="RM000002QX5001X_03_0004" fin="true">OK</down>
<right ref="RM000002QX5001X_03_0005" fin="false">NG</right>
</res>
</testgrp>
<testgrp id="RM000002QX5001X_03_0004">
<testtitle>Effect of interfering radio waves</testtitle>
</testgrp>
